<title>SWEDEN: Astra says R&amp;D spending to rise with sale.</title>
<headline>Astra says R&amp;D spending to rise with sale.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs company Astra said on Wednesday that spending on research and development (R&amp;D) would increase at the same pace as its sales.  </p>
<p>&quot;In the future (R&amp;D) will grow at about the same rate as sales,&quot; Astra's chief executive Hakan Mogren told a news conference.</p>
<p>Mogren forecast that R&amp;D costs would amount to 16-18 percent of sales in the future, while they were 18 percent of sales in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Joel Dahlberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
